<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<conversations>

	<!-- OUTRIDER (user-written 2026-08-16). First quarrier to get a voice. Unlike the miner
	     there was nothing to override: BaseHumanoid carries no ConversationScript, so before
	     this the whole guild was mute.
	     Wired on the OUTRIDER, not on the stonecarver chassis, per the profession-first ruling
	     of 2026-08-15: the profession is the face, so the bank belongs to it. The chassis needs
	     no conversation of its own as long as every carver in play has a profession, which the
	     roster currently guarantees.
	     Cleo_TerraFirma_Mole Outrider inherits this by descent, i.e. both bodies speak with one
	     voice. That is what profession-first predicts; it is not a separate ruling, and a mole
	     specific bank is one ConversationID away if the user wants the split.
	     Water ritual, trade and join-party choices arrive FREE: base Conversations.xml opens
	     with BaseConversation, "inherited by all conversations by default," which carries the
	     WaterRitualChoice and its whole subtree. Relevant here because the Quarriers ship with
	     WaterRitualJoin defaulting true, so a written bank is all recruitability needed.
	     ADDRESS TERM: "wayfarer" is the user's, written inline. That is also the only way it
	     can work; faction DefaultAddress has no conversation token, so Issachari hardcode
	     "lack-salt" in their node text exactly like this. -->
	<!-- FAREWELL RULED 2026-08-29 (user: "for the farewell, it could be rust and earth, or
	     just the default live and drink"): the guild farewell is "Rust and earth." on the
	     three carver roles (words the user's, capitalization editorial). The snapjaw miner
	     keeps his "...live and drink." below on purpose; a hired snapjaw awkwardly aping the
	     standard courtesy is its own beat, and one edit flips it if the user wants him guild-voiced. -->
	<conversation ID="Cleo_TerraFirma_Outrider">
		<node ID="Start">
			<text>
				mind the cairns, wayfarer. lest you knock one over.~
				seen a few baboons today. not one made it further than a stone's throw.
			</text>
			<choice GotoID="End">Rust and earth.</choice>
		</node>
	</conversation>

	<!-- MASON (user-written 2026-08-16). Same wiring shape as the outrider: on the role, so
	     Cleo_TerraFirma_Mole Mason inherits it by descent and both bodies speak as one mason.
	     Precedent for a trade having its own bank rather than sharing a guild one is the Stilt
	     itself: BaseMerchant points at GenericMerchant, and then every named trade on the
	     Stiltgrounds overrides it with a bank of its own. The vintner talks about wine. -->
	<conversation ID="Cleo_TerraFirma_Mason">
		<node ID="Start">
			<text>
				stones talk sometimes. just gotta listen real close, and you can hear em singing.~
				need something sculpted? man, boar, fish?~
				i sometimes wonder if the stones feel like we do. carving must hurt then, eh?~
				don't know the name of the rocks around here, but they carve just the same.
			</text>
			<choice GotoID="End">Rust and earth.</choice>
		</node>
	</conversation>

	<!-- HEWER (user-written 2026-08-16). Third role wired, same shape: on the role, so
	     Cleo_TerraFirma_Mole Hewer inherits it.
	     Two hooks in these lines that other systems already own, recorded so nobody "fixes" them:
	     the AQUIFER line is the exception to a rule the warren generator encodes (warren-lab.html
	     wetChance seals one brine pocket per warren, and wetAvoid exists so tunnels visibly bend
	     around it, hover text "diggers don't breach aquifers"). This hewer is the digger who did.
	     Brine, so the soaking is salt water.
	     The WITCHWOOD ask names an item the player stonecarver starts holding, 2 to 4 Witchwood
	     Bark out of Cleo_StartingGear_Stonecarver. Stock HaveItem and TakeItem conversation parts
	     could turn that into a real handover with no C#. DECLINED 2026-08-29 (user: "hewer's
	     witchwood is a claude proposal i'm not taking"); the line stays flavor, not a fetch hook. -->
	<conversation ID="Cleo_TerraFirma_Hewer">
		<node ID="Start">
			<text>
				smashed through a wall last week, soaked my clothes. damn aquifers.~
				overseer said we needed to square away more rock, but my back's been killing me... got any witchwood?
			</text>
			<choice GotoID="End">Rust and earth.</choice>
		</node>
	</conversation>
</conversations>
